# What :latest-patched is built from. The beta moves on its own (Dockerfile.beta's
# WINE_REF and whatever is in patches/ on main); :latest-patched does not. It stays
# on the Wine and the patch set recorded here until the beta has been tested and
# is promoted at a stable release. CI's patched job reads this file; nothing else
# does.
#
# WINE_REF      the Wine tag to build, the one the beta ran when it was tested.
# PATCHES_FROM  where patches/ comes from: "this" for the commit being built, or a
#               git tag or commit, whose patches/ is used instead (series, the
#               patches, their switches and build-wine.sh, all from that point).
#
# Promoting the beta at a release:
#   1. Set WINE_REF to the beta's and PATCHES_FROM to "this", and tag the release.
#   2. Then set PATCHES_FROM to that release tag, so a later release that changes
#      only the container keeps this Wine even after patches/ moves on for the beta.
WINE_REF=wine-11.19
PATCHES_FROM=this
